    "reason": "The changelog line [ev-636c346e8c61] only says \"toggle support for experimental channel\". The linked PR [ev-ac30ce7b1e8b] adds the motivation: standard-channel installs lack the alpha APIs, so Traefik cannot start properly, and the new knob lets users opt in to them. It also carries a \"breaking\" label. Neither text names the static-configuration option or states its default. Neither says what happens to existing users of alpha routes who do nothing. The docs that would say so (the v2-to-v3 migration guide and the static-config references listed in [ev-3857e401ecf7]) are not shown, so the subject key, the before/after values, who is exposed and the consequence cannot be written down.",
